tended:
This hand I love as I have loved a friend,
This body I tended, wept with and enjoyed;
Since there is no escape even for me

Then in my wrath I broke the bough
That I had tended so with care,
Hoping its scent should fill the air;

tender:
Their daughters took we for a pleasant prey,
Choice tender ones on whom the fathers doat.
Now they in turn have led our own away;

tent:
for dreaming in,
And at the end in the big Circus tent we sat and shook
and stewed like sin!

tenderest:
The fields are snowbound no longer;
There are little blue lakes and flags of tenderest green.
The snow has been caught up into the sky--

tenements:
Under the same dull stars.
Out of the tenements, cold as stone,
Dark figures start for work;

tentacles:
And there a seed, racked with heroic pain,
Thrust eager tentacles to sun and rain;
It climbed; it died; the old love conquered me

tendah:
Th'owin' 'way de fines' pa't.
W'y, dat skin is jes' ez tendah
An' ez juicy ez kin be;

One eye shet, an' one eye open,--dis is evah wud he said:
"Lawd, look down in tendah mussy on sich generous hea'ts ez dese;
Make us truly thankful, amen. Pass dat possum, ef you please!"

Dey 's a kin' o' doleful feelin',
Hits a tendah place,
'Long to'ds night;

tend'rest:
Permit the muse a cordial to impart;
Who can to thee their tend'rest aid refuse?
To dry thy tears how longs the heav'nly muse!

tenderer:
And yet we guessed it not;
If tenderer industriousness
Pervaded her, we thought

tendered:
She flirted and petted, or what have you;
And, tendered advice by her kind Mamma,
Her answer, I shudder to state, was "Blah!"

tendon:
ready to turn and clutch
yet never shake muscle nor nerve nor tendon;
so my mind waits
